NAME
    passwd - set an account's password

SYNOPSIS
    passwd <newpassword>
    passwd <name> <newpassword>

DESCRIPTION
    Stores a hash of <newpassword> for your OWN account (no other arguments)
    or, root only, for <name>'s account. NOT checked by 'su' or anything
    else today - see that command's own man page for why. No masked/
    interactive prompt either: there's no reliable blocking-input read
    across every host this shell runs under (a real terminal, a GUI
    TextBox-driven console, a headless test), so the new password is just a
    plain trailing argument, the same way 'bp add'/'watch add' take theirs -
    it will show up in this shell's own 'history' in plain text.

EXAMPLES
    passwd hunter2
    passwd kid hunter2
